  "description": "VUXSOY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C136 H104 Gd7 N10 O24 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.657-3.930 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.96-111.07°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C142H120Gd7N11O24.",
